"Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0747717113001181)\nciteturn7search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; # Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel David Harvey ... Number-theoretic transform\n\n## Journal of Symbolic Computation\n\nDate: January 2014\n\nPages: 113-119\n\nVolume: Volume 60\n\n## Published by: Elsevier\n\n# Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel David Harvey\n\nShow more\n\nView PDF Download full issue\n\nCite\n\nAdd to Mendeley\n\nShare\n\n10.1016/j.jsc.2013.09.002\n\nMore actions\n\n  * Article\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe show how to improve the efficiency of the computation of fast Fourier transforms over {\\mathbf{F}}_{p} where p is a word-sized prime. Our main technique is optimisation of the basic arithmetic, in effect decreasing the total number of reductions modulo p, by making use of a redundant representation for integers modulo p. We give performance results showing a significant improvement over Shoupʼs NTL library.\n\n## Keywords\n\nNumber-theoretic transform\n\n;\n\nFast Fourier transform\n\n;\n\nModular arithmetic\n\n;\n\nEfficient algorithm--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFaster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms (https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.2926)\nciteturn7academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.5 years ago; Title: Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms\nAuthors: David Harvey\nTitle: Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms\nAuthors: David Harvey\nDate: Mon May 14 01:34:22 2012\n\nWe show how to improve the efficiency of the computation of fast Fourier transforms over F_p where p is a word-sized prime. Our main technique is optimisation of the basic arithmetic, in effect decreasing the total number of reductions modulo p, by making use of a redundant representation for integers modulo 