c for number-theoretic transforms\" by David Harvey. ...   * Speeding up the number theoretic transform by Longa and Naehrig\n\n## \"Matters Computational\" (aka fxtbook)\n\nJoerg Arndt's tour de force on computer arithmetic algorithms. He's been in the business for a while.\n\n  * Link\n\n## Binary Splitting\n\nThere are a few references on binary splitting. The canonical one for me is the Haible paper.\n\n  * Haible & Papanikolaou\n\n  * Gourdon & Sebah\n\n## Number-Theoretic Transforms\n\n  * Link: \"Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms\" by David Harvey. These slides are generally useful for the implementation of NTTs. Includes Shoup's modular arithmetic trick.\n\n  * Link: A simple NTT tutorial going through the basics.\n\n  * Link: Mikko Tommila's notes on the NTT.\n\n  * Speeding up the number theoretic transform by Longa and Naehrig\n\n  * The FFT - an algorithm the whole family can use: Just a fun paper title. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpeedup of discrete Fourier transform by efficient modular arithmetic - Zhang - 2022 - Concurrency and Computation: Practice and Experience - Wiley Online Library (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/cpe.6564)\nciteturn7search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago;   * 6 Harvey D, Hoeven J, Lecerf G. ... The fast Fourier transform in a finite field. ... The computation of Image: urn:x-wiley:15320626:media:cpe6564:cpe6564-math-0255 to 29,360,000 decimal digits using Borweins' quartically convergent algorithm. ... Faster arithmetic for number-theoretic transforms.\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 31 Cormen TH, Leiserson CE, Rivest RL, Stein C. Introduction to Algorithms. 3rd ed. MIT Press; 2009.\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 32 Montgomery PL. Modular multiplication without trial division. Math Comput. 1985; 44(170): 519-521.\n\nWeb of Science® Google Scholar\n\n  * 33 Karatsuba AA, Ofman YP. Multiplication of many-digital numbers by a